        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:18:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124349,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Chronically sun-exposed skin is typically affected, with a predilection for the face and the arms.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:18:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124350,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Large cell acanthomas appear as well-circumscribed tan to brown macules, typically measuring &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mm {24917472; 12581141}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:18:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124351,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fair-skinned, middle-aged to elderly adults are mainly affected {24917472; 12581141}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:18:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124352,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Large cell acanthomas are linked to chronic ultraviolet (UV) radiation exposure.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:18:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124353,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is considerable overlap with solar lentigo with respect to the expression of keratin and of antiapoptotic and proliferative markers {24917472}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:18:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124354,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:18:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124355,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "<p>Large cell acanthomas are sharply delineated from the adjacent normal epidermis and characterized by epidermal flattening and overlying basket-weave hyperkeratosis. They are composed of enlarged keratinocytes with nuclei up to twice the size of those of adjacent normal keratinocytes. The lesional keratinocytes contain abundant cytoplasm and the nuclear contours are smooth and regular. There is no nuclear pleomorphism, and mitotic figures are rare. Hyperpigmentation of the basal cell layer is frequently observed. There are often admixed or adjacent changes of solar lentigo.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Actinic keratoses show squamous dysplasia affecting the lower and mid epidermal layers, often associated with overlying parakeratosis. Lentigo maligna is characterized by confluent growth of single junctional melanocytes, which may be highlighted by immunohistochemistry for melan-A or SOX10.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:18:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
